#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:47
msgid ""
"image:dark-elves/logo.webp[width=111,height=92,float=\"right\"] Over five "
"thousand years ago a great civil war erupted amongst the Elven Kingdoms on "
"the island-continent of Ulthuan. Upon one side were the supporters of the "
"Phoenix King whilst upon the other were the supporters of Malekith Lord of "
"Nagarythe. Malekith was the son of Aenarion – the first and greatest of the "
"Phoenix Kings – and his mother was a powerful and influential sorceress "
"called Morathi. Many fair-minded Elves believed that Malekith was the "
"rightful heir to the Phoenix throne. They remembered that he had fought "
"valiantly against the daemontides of Chaos and his noble appearance recalled "
"that of his mighty father."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:60
msgid ""
"Morathi nurtured a huge ambition to rule and her son was to provide her with "
"the means to achieve power. She was prepared to go to any ends to realise "
"her ambitions and was fearless and proud even in the face of the gods "
"themselves. She was also skilled in all the arts of magic and especially in "
"the lore of daemons and all manner of necromancy. Unbeknown to the common "
"folk, her mastery of the dark powers earned her the admiration of many who "
"believed that such forces could be harnessed and used to empower the Elves. "
"Her followers grew in number and she became so bold that the forbidden gods "
"were worshipped openly in the temples of Nagarythe and many flocked to join "
"the new cults."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Thanks in part to his mother’s efforts Malekith’s cause prospered even as "
"darkness and corruption spread amongst the elves. As Malekith’s influence "
"grew he came to believe himself indestructible. So certain was he of his "
"divine destiny that he decided to pass into the flame of Asuryan to prove "
"his right to rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:77
msgid ""
"By this rite the greatest of the Elven gods grants power and divine "
"authority to the true kings of Ulthuan. But the Elven gods were not bowed by "
"Morathi’s power and the flame rejected her son. Malekith was not killed, but "
"his body was badly burned and afterwards he made a suit of black armour that "
"he wears to this day. Seriously weakened, blackened of body, his mind warped "
"by pain and resentment, Malekith gave up all pretence of rightful lordship "
"and chose instead to impose his will by force of arms alone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:91
msgid ""
"The long, bitter and bloody war that followed became known as The Sundering "
"– for its result was to divide the [.edit]#Elven# race.  From then on the "
"High Elves of Ulthuan, the Wood Elves of the abandoned Elf colonies in the "
"Old World, and the Dark Elves of Malekith would develop separately. The Dark "
"Elves were eventually driven out of Ulthuan. The land of Nagarythe and a "
"great part of the other western lands of Ulthuan were torn apart by great "
"magical upheavals as the rival sides battled for supremacy. Nagarythe "
"finally sank beneath the waves.  Malekith and his supporters fled to the "
"northern part of the New World where they founded their own kingdom in exile "
"upon the borderlands of Chaos. This they named Naggaroth – which means Land "
"of Chill in Elvish."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:104
msgid ""
"From his icy realm Malekith broods over his lost kingdom and weaves dark "
"spells against his enemies. His ships harass those of the High Elves, his "
"raiders harry the coasts of Ulthuan and the Old World, whilst his generals "
"plan to return to their homeland and win the Elven Kingdoms for their dark "
"master. In the land of Naggaroth the Dark Elves raised temples to all manner "
"of blood-thirsty Daemons. Witch Elves roam the night searching for "
"sacrifices, breaking into home to steal away children, and murdering those "
"foolish enough to walk abroad beneath the stars. Under the evil gaze of "
"Morathi thousands are sacrificed upon the altars of Khaine while to this day "
"she preserves her unholy youth by bathing in the blood of innocents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dark Elf army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$dark-elves.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[crossbowmen-and-dark-riders,†1]]1. Crossbowmen and Dark Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:125
msgid ""
"These units are equipped with the repeating crossbow. These units shoot once "
"at ranges up to 30cm and twice at ranges up to 15cm. A unit of three stands "
"would therefore shoot 6 Attacks at a target within 15cm and 3 Attacks at a "
"target at greater ranges. Units may shoot at enemies that charge them – in "
"which case they shoot 1 Attack per stand regardless of range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[witch-elves,†2]]2. Witch Elves"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:134
msgid ""
"A unit of Witch Elves always uses its initiative to charge an enemy if "
"possible and cannot be given orders instead. Witch Elves never use their "
"initiative to evade. The unit cannot be driven back by shooting and never "
"roll for drive backs. If victorious in combat they must pursue or advance "
"where possible. Witch Elves are unaffected by enemies that cause terror in "
"combat and do not suffer the usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[cold-one-knights,†3]]3. Cold One Knights"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:141
msgid ""
"Such is their unthinking instinct to take a bite out of anything that "
"passes, Cold One Knights has an Attack value bonus of +1 in the first round "
"of each combat when fighting to the front, i.e. the Cold One Knights’ stand "
"has to touch the enemy in arc of sight with its frontal edge and/or frontal "
"corners (including contact by frontal corner only)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:145
msgid ""
"For the same reason Cold One Knights cannot form brigades except with other "
"units of Cold One Knights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[harpies,†4]]4. Harpies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[war-hydra,†5]]5. War Hydra"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:153
msgid ""
"War Hydras are so aggressive that they cannot be included as part of a "
"brigade not even with other War Hydras."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:155
msgid "They cause terror in their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:159
msgid ""
"The War Hydra can breath fire with a range of 20cm and 2 Attacks that are "
"worked out in the normal way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:165
msgid ""
"Once all hits have been struck for that round, and assuming it has not been "
"slain, the War Hydra automatically regenerates 1 hit that it suffered that "
"round. A hit that is inflicted and subsequently regenerated still counts "
"towards the results for that round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:166
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[elven-bolt-thrower,†6]]6. Elven Bolt Thrower"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:168
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:155
msgid ""
"Rules for the Elven Bolt Thrower are described in the xref:rules:artillery-"
"and-machines.adoc#elven-bolt-thrower[Artillery and Machines] section in the "
"Rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[general,†7]]7. General"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:182
msgid ""
"Dark Elf commanders are masters of manipulation and cruelty – this makes "
"them uncompromising in their dealings with subordinates! If a Dark Elf Hero "
"or Sorceress rolls a double 6 when issuing orders then the General must "
"either lose 1 level of Command value (i.e. drop from 10 to 9) or execute the "
"failed underling – in which case the character is removed as a casualty but "
"does not count towards the enemy’s victory points.  In addition, if the "
"General rolls a ‘blunder’ (i.e. a double 6) then the General automatically "
"loses 1 level. Regardless of these penalties a General can only drop 2 "
"levels (to a minimum of 8)  after which all subordinates who blunder are "
"executed and any ‘blunders’ rolled by the General merely end the phase as "
"normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[manticore,†8]]8. Manticore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:185
msgid "Generals, Heroes and the Sorceress can ride a Manticore."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:188
msgid "The Manticore can fly increasing the rider’s movement to 100cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:191
msgid "An extra +2 Attacks are added to those of the rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:193
msgid "A unit joined by the character causes Terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[cauldron-of-blood,†9]]9. Cauldron of Blood"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:198
msgid ""
"A Sorceress can have a Cauldron of Blood. The army can only ever include one "
"Cauldron of Blood and it can only be included if there is at least 1 unit of "
"Witch Elves in the army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:201
msgid ""
"A Sorceress with a Cauldron of Blood suffers a movement reduction to 30cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:208
msgid ""
"The Cauldron of Blood adds +2 Attacks to the Sorceress and can be used to "
"add +1 to the Sorceress’ dice roll to cast a spell once per battle. The "
"player must announce that the Cauldron of Blood’s spell bonus is being used "
"before rolling the dice to determine if the spell is cast."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:212
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dark Elf spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:215
#, no-wrap
msgid "Doom Bolt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:221
msgid ""
"_A bolt of pure malicious darkness arcs from the Sorcerer’s fingertip and "
"stabs towards the foes of the Dark Elves._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:227
msgid ""
"Draw an imaginary line 30cm long from the Sorceress’s stand in any direction "
"you wish. The line will pass through any intervening units but not beyond "
"terrain that would normally stop a missile shot, e.g. over the crest of a "
"hill, more than 2cm of woodland, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:236
msgid ""
"Each unit under the line takes three shooting attacks worked out in the "
"usual way. Note that this spell can easily effect several units and will "
"affect all units that fall beneath the line (including your own). Unengaged "
"units can be driven back by a Doom Bolt as with ordinary shooting (even "
"including friends).  Engaged units cannot be driven back by the Doom Bolt "
"but carry over any hits scored into the first round of combat; any hits "
"scored count as having been struck in the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:238
#, no-wrap
msgid "Black Horror"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:241
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/orcs.adoc:170
msgid "[.cost]#6+ to cast# [.points]#Range 50cm#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:244
msgid ""
"_A whirling vortex of dark enemy surrounds and drags its victims into the "
"infernal realms of Khaine the Lord of Murder._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:250
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon an enemy unit the Sorceress can see and which is "
"not engaged in combat. The units suffers 4 Attacks with no saves for Armour. "
"A unit that takes hits from the Black Horror is not driven back as a result "
"– the whirling vortex sucks its victims down affording them no chance to "
"avoid it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:252
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dominian"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:258
msgid ""
"_Upon invoking the curse of the foul god Khaine an unnatural and unbearable "
"agony suffuses the body of his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:261
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Sorceress can see it or not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:264
msgid ""
"The spell takes affect until the end of the opposing player’s next turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:269
msgid ""
"Whilst the spell lasts the unit cannot charge and if engaged in combat will "
"not pursue or advance. Even units that are otherwise obliged to charge, "
"pursue, or advance will not do so if affected by Dominion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "Soul Stealer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:274
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/kislev.adoc:220
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/lizardmen.adoc:279
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/norse.adoc:224
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:164
msgid "[.cost]#5+ to cast# [.points]#Range N/A#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:277
msgid ""
"_Invoking the daemons of the abyss the Sorcerer tears the very souls from "
"his enemies._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:281
msgid ""
"The Sorceress can cast this spell if she has joined a unit in combat. The "
"spell can be cast on any single enemy unit that is touching the unit the "
"Sorceress has joined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:288
msgid ""
"The target unit takes three attacks worked out in the usual way. Targets get "
"no armour saving throws when they suffer hits from the Soul Stealer – all "
"Armour values count as 0. Any hits scored are carried over into the first "
"round of combat and count as having been struck in the first round for "
"purposes of working out combat results."
msgstr ""
